1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:05,000
Two Pairs of Hands Mumbai and Pune, 2035.

2
00:00:05,467 --> 00:00:09,500
Every skill on Knack belongs to someone.

3
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:14,000
The one who records

4
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:18,000
Twenty-two years in commercial kitchens. His wrists are starting to fail him. When his hands stop, everything they know stops with them.

5
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:25,100
Knack pays experts to record their hands. Arjun applies.

6
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:31,733
Only verified experts can record. Knack checks his kitchens, his guild level, and his hands.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,133
Every hour anyone streams his hands, he keeps 30%: ₹555.

8
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,333
He chooses who may never use them.

9
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:47,067
And he signs one clause without reading it twice.

10
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:54,867
For six months, two patches record him through 156 dinner services. He just cooks.

11
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:59,067
Knack is watching his right wrist too.

12
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:03,700
1,352 hours of his hands.

13
00:01:04,767 --> 00:01:08,700
Knack keeps only his best hours.

14
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:15,533
212 hours are cut: tiredness, tremor, mistakes. Most of the tremor came from his right wrist.

15
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:22,067
Certified. His skill is now a product.

16
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:26,400
His hands are in the vault.

17
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:29,400
Five months later.

18
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:34,800
Every minute someone streams his hands, he is paid. ₹3,10,245 in October.

19
00:01:35,267 --> 00:01:40,000
Right now, his hands are working in kitchens across India.

20
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:43,933
He no longer works full services.

21
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,333
In August, Knack launched a cheaper knife skill: ₹340 an hour.

22
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:52,333
It was built from 3,100 sessions. 412 of those hours were his.

23
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:56,933
Clause 14.2. His own hands are being used to replace him.

24
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:01,433
The one who rents

25
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:04,833
She has cooked at home all her life. On Monday she starts a trial shift in a restaurant kitchen. She has never held a knife the way chefs do.

26
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:16,167
Her cousin sends her a link: a skin patch that lets you rent an expert’s hands, by the hour.

27
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:26,233
She designs the shell it wears.

28
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:30,200
₹48,900 for the patch. It is hers to keep. The skills are not.

29
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:34,767
She has eight days. She pays extra for a drone drop.

30
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:37,700
Her shell is printed overnight.

31
00:02:38,167 --> 00:02:40,700
The drone lands on the terrace.

32
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,867
She taps her phone on the box lid. The patch knows it is hers.

33
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:54,300
A small test pulse. The patch learns how her muscles answer.

34
00:02:54,767 --> 00:02:58,200
Knack already has a profile of her: her health record, her smart ring…

35
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:04,933
…and her new employer, who pays 20% of her plan and will see every hour she streams. She leaves it on.

36
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:16,267
In the vault, she finds a knife skill recorded in Mumbai.

37
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:24,333
She has never met him. She chooses his hands.

38
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:29,667
Her plan is built from her body: short sessions, long rests.

39
00:03:30,133 --> 00:03:36,967
She confirms she knows what streaming does to her, and pays.

40
00:03:37,433 --> 00:03:40,800
She skips the safety guide. Nine in ten people do.

41
00:03:41,267 --> 00:03:44,200
Her trial shift starts at ten.

42
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:51,733
For 45 minutes, her hands move like his.

43
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:09,433
Keeping the 18% that stays would cost ₹83,300. ₹24,990 of it would go to Arjun.

44
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:12,767
She lets it fade.

45
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:17,467
Both sides of one session

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,533
In Mumbai, Arjun’s phone lights up.

47
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,933
A cook in Pune. He will never know her name.

48
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:36,433
Asha gets the job. Her employer can see every hour she streams. Her own hands, without the patch, are a little less steady than they were a week ago.

49
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:43,933
Arjun earns ₹416 for 45 minutes he didn’t work. His right wrist aches. The skill built from his hours costs less than he does.

50
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:49,933
Who owns a skill once it has been in your hands?

51
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:55,433
Get the knack. Not a real product.
